+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI agents in 2026 for developers?
+If you want developer-focused options, start with `open-swe`, `goose`, `plandex`, and `qwen-code`. For building your own stack, `adk-python`, `adk-go`, `TEN-framework`, and `voltagent` are stronger foundations than UI-only products.
+
+### Which open source AI agents can I self-host?
+`LibreChat`, `Khoj`, `DB-GPT`, `IntentKit`, `Browserable`, and `R2R` all support self-hosted use cases in different ways. Some are full platforms, while others are infrastructure layers or focused frameworks.
+
+### Are all tools in this list public GitHub repositories?
+Yes. Every entry in this README points to a public `github.com` repository. Proprietary SaaS-only tools, closed hosted services, and products without a public GitHub repo were excluded.
+
+### What is the best open source AI agent for browser automation?
+For browser-heavy work, look first at `UI-TARS-desktop`, `nanobrowser`, `browser-agent`, `steel-browser`, and `browserable`. The right pick depends on whether you want GUI control, an extension model, or self-hosted browser infrastructure.
+
+### What is the best open source AI agent for coding tasks?
+`open-swe` is strongest for internal coding-agent architecture, `goose` is excellent for terminal-centric workflows, `plandex` is useful for larger codebases, and `qwen-code` is a strong open terminal agent. Teams wanting a framework instead of an opinionated tool should compare the ADK repos.
+
+### How did you handle categories with too few repositories?
+When a subcategory had fewer than five strong candidates, I did not create a thin standalone section just to pad the list. Instead, those projects were merged into a broader category and the gap is documented here as intentional curation.
+
+### Are the stars, languages, and licenses verified from GitHub?
+Yes. The list was assembled from GitHub repository research and GitHub repo pages, and each entry includes stars, primary language, license type, and recent commit activity taken from GitHub data.
